{
  "sn22.81:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.81 ",
  "sn22.81:0.2": "8. Bitable ",
  "sn22.81:0.3": "At Pārileyyaka ",
  "sn22.81:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Kosambī in Ghosita’s monastery. ",
  "sn22.81:1.2": "Then the Buddha robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Kosambī for alms. ",
  "sn22.81:1.3": "After the meal, on his return from almsround, he set his lodgings in order himself. Taking his bowl and robe, without informing his supporters or taking leave of the mendicant Saṅgha, he set out to go wandering alone, with no companion. ",
  "sn22.81:2.1": "Then, not long after the Buddha had left, one of the mendicants went to Venerable Ānanda and told him what had happened. ",
  "sn22.81:2.2": "",
  "sn22.81:2.3": "Ānanda said, “Reverend, when the Buddha leaves like this it means he wants to stay alone. ",
  "sn22.81:2.4": "At this time no one should follow him.” ",
  "sn22.81:3.1": "Then the Buddha, traveling stage by stage, arrived at Pārileyyaka, ",
  "sn22.81:3.2": "where he stayed at the root of a sacred sal tree. ",
  "sn22.81:3.3": "Then several mendicants went up to Venerable Ānanda and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "sn22.81:3.4": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, they sat down to one side and said to him, ",
  "sn22.81:3.5": "“Reverend, it’s been a long time since we’ve heard a Dhamma talk from the Buddha. ",
  "sn22.81:3.6": "We wish to hear a Dhamma talk from the Buddha.” ",
  "sn22.81:4.1": "Then Venerable Ānan